{"text": "Judy L. Norton-Eledge\n\nQualifications: 1990 Public School Administration, University of Alaska/Anchorage\n1989 Masters of Teaching: Emphasis HRD, AK Pacific University/Anchorage 1979 BS:\nElementary Education, Sul Ross University: Alpine, TX\n\nExperience:\n2003-Current: Owner, Educational Consultant Contract Business. Have worked\nwith low performing schools throughout Alaska. Expertise in Professional\nLearning Communities in the areas of reading and math.\n\n2009-2012: AK State Audit Team and one of first seven Technical Coaches hired to\nwork with low performing school districts in Alaska.\n\n2008-2012: Alaska Reading Online Reading Class. Developed online class to train\nteachers in the area of reading.\n\n2005-2015: AK State Training of Trainers in the area of data analysis in school\nimprovement.\n\n1999-2004: Principal, Director of Curriculum & Instruction, District Testing\nCoordinator, Copper River School District\n\n1997-1999: Assistant Principal, North Slope Borough School District\n1993-1997: Migrant Education Supervisor, Anchorage School District\n1981-1993: Elementary School Teacher, Anchorage School District\n\n1972-1981 Elementary School Teacher, Del Rio Texas\n\nCommunity Service\n\nAlaska State Commission on Juvenile Justice\nAlaska State Excellence in Public Service\nFar View Home Owners Association President\nBoard of Directors: Learning Disabilities Association of\nAlaska\n\nCommissioner: Municipality of Anchorage/ Health & Human\nServices Commission",
